<article class="env-remark" id="0DK8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DK8">Remark <span data-tag="0DK8">75.17.4</span> <span class="named">(Variant with support)</span>.</a>  Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated algebraic space. Let $T \subset |X|$ be a closed subset such that $|X| \setminus T$ is quasi-compact. The analogue of Theorem <a href="/tag/09MC" data-tag="09MC">75.17.3</a> holds for $D_{\mathit{QCoh}, T}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. This follows from the exact same argument as in the proof of the theorem, using Lemmas <a href="/tag/0AEC" data-tag="0AEC">75.15.6</a> and <a href="/tag/0AED" data-tag="0AED">75.16.3</a> and a variant of Lemma <a href="/tag/09MA" data-tag="09MA">75.17.1</a> with supports. If we ever need this, we will precisely state the result here and give a detailed proof. </p>
</article>